# Quality & Consistency Checks

Run this checklist and flag any issue to the user before marking a task done.

### Token Check

- [ ] Zero hardcoded hex in new component SCSS — colors via the CSS custom properties in `src/styles/settings.scss` (`--color-primary`, `--color-gray-*`, `--color-bg`, `--color-text`). Sass color functions use the `$`-mirrors (`$primary`).
- [ ] Container sizes and type via tokens (`--size-container-*`, `--font-*`). Add a token to `settings.scss` rather than a one-off raw value.
- [ ] Zero raw breakpoint values in `@media` — use `b-up` / `b-d` / `b-btw` / `b-o` (rule 12).

### State Completeness

Check these states exist in the design AND in code. Flag any missing from either.

- Default / rest
- Hover — interactive elements (desktop only — gate with `@media (hover: hover)`)
- Focus / focus-visible — interactive elements (keyboard reachable)
- Pressed / active — interactive elements
- Disabled — `disabled` for native controls, `aria-disabled="true"` for custom
- Loading / busy — elements that trigger async (`aria-busy="true"`)
- Error — inputs, forms, data displays
- Empty — lists, data displays

**Flag example**: "The design has no error state for the newsletter input. Should I build it with a red border and an error message below as the default?"

### Merging Check

If two components being built are structurally identical with minor style differences, flag it and recommend a `variant` prop.

### Text flexibility

For any component that contains text:

1. Does it handle text that is ~2× longer without breaking layout?
2. Does it handle text that wraps to 2 lines without breaking layout?

Apply unconditionally:

- No fixed `width` / `height` on text containers. Use `min-width` / `min-height` if a minimum is required.
- Allow wrapping unless the design explicitly says "single line only" — then `white-space: nowrap; overflow: hidden; text-overflow: ellipsis;` and a tooltip if context is lost.
- Icon + label rows: label flexes, icon pinned with `flex-shrink: 0`.
- Avoid `position: absolute` for text labels.

### Accessibility

No a11y linter runs in this repo, so these checks are manual.

- Prefer semantic HTML first (`<button>`, `<a>`, `<input>`, `<nav>`, `<dialog>`). ARIA only when no native element fits.
- All interactive elements reachable via keyboard. Visible focus indicator (no `outline: none` without a replacement).
- `alt` on every `<Image>` / `<img>`; empty `alt=""` for decorative images.
- `aria-label` on icon-only buttons. `aria-describedby` for error/help text on inputs.
- Decorative SVGR icons: `aria-hidden="true"`.
- Color contrast: minimum 4.5:1 for body text, 3:1 for large text and interactive boundaries.

### Props Consistency

Props that appear in more than one component must use identical names and types:

```
disabled: boolean
isLoading: boolean        (not: loading, pending, busy)
onClick: () => void       (not: onPress, onTap)
variant: string union     (not: type, kind, mode)
size: 'small' | 'medium' | 'large'
className?: string        (always accepted on the root)
```

### className Composition

`classnames` aliased as `cn` is the only helper. See `14-classnames-cn-alias.mdc`.
